@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy | It's a Budget</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="The It's a Budget privacy policy explains the data used to provide budgeting, authentication, notifications, and optional Plaid bank connections." />
</HeadContent>

<article class="public-page legal-page">
    <p class="public-page-kicker">PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Effective July 29, 2026</p>

    <p>
        This policy describes how It's a Budget collects, uses, stores, and
        shares information when you use the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Information you provide</h2>
    <p>
        The service may store account profile information, household budget
        memberships, accounts, balances, transactions, payees, categories,
        recurring budget items, attachments, notification preferences, and
        other information you enter. Administrators may configure an email
        address for notifications and an external identity for sign-in.
    </p>

    <h2>Information from connected financial institutions</h2>
    <p>
        If you choose to connect an eligible institution, It's a Budget uses
        Plaid Link. Plaid may collect institution credentials and account
        information under Plaid's own privacy policy. It's a Budget does not
        receive or store the username and password you use at your financial
        institution.
    </p>
    <p>
        The service may receive institution and account identifiers, account
        names and balances, transaction details, connection status, and data
        needed to refresh or disconnect the connection. Connected transaction
        data is staged for reconciliation with your checkbook.
    </p>

    <h2>Authentication and technical data</h2>
    <p>
        The service uses essential cookies to maintain authentication and the
        interactive application session. Server logs may contain timestamps,
        request paths, coarse connection information, authentication outcomes,
        and errors needed for security and reliability. The service does not
        use advertising cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Provide ledgers, forecasts, budgets, reports, sharing, and exports.</li>
        <li>Authenticate users and enforce account and household permissions.</li>
        <li>Sync and reconcile connected-account data you request.</li>
        <li>Send notifications you opt into.</li>
        <li>Back up, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How information is shared</h2>
    <p>
        Information is shared only as needed to operate the service, comply
        with law, protect the service and its users, or carry out a request you
        make. Service providers may include Plaid for optional bank
        connections, the configured identity provider for external sign-in,
        and the configured email provider for notifications. It's a Budget does
        not sell personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
        Information is retained while needed to operate the account, meet
        security and backup requirements, resolve disputes, and comply with
        legal obligations. Deletion from active systems may not immediately
        remove copies from limited-retention backups. See the
        <a href="/data-deletion">data-deletion instructions</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
        The service uses HTTPS in production, access controls, and operational
        safeguards intended to protect information. No internet service can
        guarantee absolute security. See the <a href="/security">Security and
        Data Use page</a> for more detail.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
        The service is not directed to children under 13, and the operator does
        not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        Material changes will be reflected on this page with a new effective
        date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        Privacy questions and requests can be submitted using the
        <a href="/contact">contact instructions</a>.
    </p>
</article>
